              {
                "publicationCitation": {
                  "typeName": "publicationCitation",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "Filioglou D, Valenzuela-Lamas S, Patterson WP, Pena LD, Presslee S, Timsic S, Delgado Huertas A, Prummel, W and Çakirlar C (2024) Where did the herds go? Combining zooarchaeological and isotopic data to examine animal management in ancient Thessaly (Greece). PLoS ONE 19(10): e0299788. <a href=https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0299788</a>\n<br> <br>\nFilioglou, D. (2023). <i>Pastoralism in context: a zooarchaeological study from the Classical through the Hellenistic Periods in southern Thessaly in Greece.</i> University of Groningen. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.33612/diss.662423699\">https://doi.org/10.33612/diss.662423699</a>\n<br> <br>\nFilioglou, D., & Çakırlar, C. (2023). Animal Economy in Hellenistic Greece: A Zooarchaeological Study from Pherae (Thessaly). <i>Journal of Field Archaeology, 48</i>(3), 227-244. Advance online publication. <a  href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080/00934690.2022.2163782\">https://doi.org/10.1080/00934690.2022.2163782</a>\n<br> <br>\nFilioglou, D., Prummel, W., & Çakirlar, C. (2021). Animal husbandry in Classical and Hellenistic Thessaly (Central Greece): A zooarchaeological perspective from Almiros. <i>Journal of Archaeological Science: Reports, 39</i>, Article 103164. <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jasrep.2021.103164\">https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jasrep.2021.103164</a>"
